    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite (`./mvnw test`) reports `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 the acceptance tests are the only concrete test class in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion to a soft-delete. Changes:\n\n**Domain model** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`\n- Added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`, defaults to `false`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)`. A newly created owner is `false` since the create path never sets it.\n\n**Database schema** \u2014 added a `deleted` column with a `DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` to all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) so existing seed rows in `data.sql` default to not-deleted. Tests run on the `hsqldb` profile.\n\n**API contract** \u2014 `resources/openapi.yml`\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the flag and MapStruct maps it automatically. This is what `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns.\n\n**Delete behavior** \u2014 `service/ClinicServiceImpl.deleteOwner`\n- Now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s the owner (retaining the row) instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.deleteOwner` returns `200 OK` with the (now-deleted) owner body \u2014 a 2xx response as required.\n\n**Duplicate/identity checks** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.activeOwners()`\n- This is the documented single scope for the duplicate and identity rules (household-duplicate, soft-duplicate, customer-code de-dup, namesake count). It now filters out `deleted` owners, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted. The count-based capacity/daily-limit rules (not duplicate/identity checks) are intentionally unchanged, per the spec's wording.\n\n`GET /api/owners/{id}` still returns soft-deleted owners because `findById` does an unfiltered lookup \u2014 matching the requirement that the owner remains readable with `deleted: true`.",
